# HSMS UI Consistency Rules

Apply these standards to every list/dashboard page in the Housing Society Management System.

## 1. Page Layout Order
1. Page title (h1, text-2xl font-bold text-foreground)
2. Description (text-muted-foreground mt-1)
3. Summary cards (grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4)
4. ActionBar (left: filters/export/refresh, right: Add New)
5. Filter section (if applicable) with FilterSection component
6. Data table (text-sm, consistent padding)

Wrap content in: `<div className="space-y-6">`

## 2. Summary Cards
- Use `SummaryCard` from `@/components/shared/SummaryCard`
- Pass `icon` as Lucide icon component (e.g. `icon={Users}`)
- Use `iconBgClassName="bg-{color}-500/20"` and `iconClassName="text-{color}-400"`
- Use `gradient="from-{color}-500/10 to-transparent"` for glass effect
- Every page must have at least 1 summary card; typically 4

## 3. ActionBar
- Import from `@/components/shared/PageTemplate`
- **left**: Reset Filters, Export, Refresh, bulk actions (use `variant="glass"` buttons)
- **right**: Add New button (use `variant="primary"` button)
- Use `size="sm"` and icon `className="size-4"` on buttons

## 4. Button Variants
- **primary**: Add New, Create - gradient, emerald/teal
- **glass**: Export, Refresh, Reset Filters, Import - glass effect with border-white/10

## 5. Table
- Use `text-sm` for table content
- Cell padding: `px-4 py-3`
- Header: `font-semibold`, `bg-white/5`
- Rows: `hover:bg-white/5`, alternating `even:bg-white/[0.02]`

## 6. Filter Section
- Use `FilterSection` from `@/components/shared/FilterSection` for labeled filter groups
- Use `FilterChip` for active filters display
- Every filter must have clear label (e.g. "Filter by Status")

## 7. Spacing
- Section gap: `space-y-6`
- Card grid: `gap-4`
- Button groups: `gap-3`
- Card padding: `p-6`
